<UserControl
	xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
	xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
	xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
	xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
	xmlns:vm="using:Mesen.ViewModels"
	xmlns:l="using:Mesen.Localization"
	mc:Ignorable="d" d:DesignWidth="440" d:DesignHeight="160"
	x:DataType="vm:PlayerAudioSettingsViewModel"
	x:Class="Mesen.Views.PlayerAudioSettingsView"
>
	<!--G.4 (W-P8): Settings › Audio - three rows in Display's pattern: the
	Sound switch, Volume, the Output device popup; Menu sounds (#1105) is a fourth only while the host can play it. A device set in Options
	that is not enumerated now stays the current item. Equalizer, reverb,
	crossfeed, latency and sample rate are "More in Options…".
	#1123 (ADR-0269 Decision 6): a row is a Grid whose first column is Auto and
	whose last is the star, not a DockPanel with a right-docked control and the
	label left to eat what is left: at 1.5 in 512x505 the page gives a row about
	220 px, and a 200 px popup (or a 150 px slider beside its 34 px readout)
	docked right left the label 20 px to draw 91 px of text in. An Auto column
	holds the label at the width its text needs, and the control takes the rest,
	up to the width ADR-0249 draws it at (150, 200) and no further. The readout
	keeps its own Auto column, so the slider shrinks first.
	#1145 review: the cap is on the *column* (`1000*` + `MaxWidth`), written
	nowhere else, and the control stretches into that column. Two other shapes
	lose at 1024x640, a size where nothing moves. A `Width` on the control
	cannot shrink at all - Avalonia's MinMax makes it both the minimum and the
	maximum - so at 1.5 in 512x505 it forced its full 150/200 into a column
	that had less and was drawn over its own label. A `MaxWidth` on the control
	in a plain `*` column keeps the cap but centres the control the moment the
	column is wider than that cap (Avalonia arranges Stretch and Center from
	the same origin), so the popups and the sliders sat mid-row with the
	leftover split around them. With the cap on the column the control's box
	*is* the column's box: as wide as the room up to the cap, and flush at its
	right edge because there is no leftover inside the column to centre it in.
	`HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"` on every one of these controls is
	load-bearing rather than a restatement of a default: Avalonia's ComboBox is
	Left by default, and a Left child is arranged at min(its column, its own
	DesiredSize), so the closed popup would shrink to whatever text it happens
	to hold - 36 px for a device list the host has not enumerated - and float
	mid-row. The star column before the capped one takes the leftover, which is
	what keeps the control against its readout (or the row's own right edge),
	where ADR-0249 draws it. Two tests hold this at 1024x640: this class's
	InterfaceSizeLayoutTests on the cap *and* that right edge, and
	PlayerThemeSettingsRenderTests on the 200/150 at factor 1.-->
	<Border Name="AudioSettingsGroup" Classes="group inset" VerticalAlignment="Top">
		<StackPanel XYFocus.NavigationModes="Enabled">
			<Grid Classes="setting-row" ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*">
				<TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Classes="callout" Text="{l:Translate lblAudioSound}" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
				<ToggleSwitch Grid.Column="1" Name="chkAudioEnabled" IsChecked="{Binding Config.EnableAudio}" HorizontalAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
			</Grid>
			<Separator Classes="row-hairline" />
			<Grid Classes="setting-row">
				<Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
					<ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
					<ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
					<ColumnDefinition Width="1000*" MaxWidth="150" />
					<ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
				</Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
				<TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Classes="callout" Text="{l:Translate lblAudioVolume}" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
				<Slider Grid.Column="2" Name="sldAudioVolume" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" Minimum="0" Maximum="100" Value="{Binding Volume}" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
				<TextBlock Grid.Column="3" Name="txtAudioVolume" Classes="callout" Width="34" TextAlignment="Right" Text="{Binding Volume, StringFormat={}{0:0}}" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
			</Grid>
			<Separator Classes="row-hairline" />
			<Grid Classes="setting-row">
				<Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
					<ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
					<ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
					<ColumnDefinition Width="1000*" MaxWidth="200" />
				</Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
				<TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Classes="callout" Text="{l:Translate lblAudioOutput}" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
				<ComboBox Grid.Column="2" Name="cboAudioDevice" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" Classes="popup" ItemsSource="{Binding Devices}" SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedDevice}" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
			</Grid>
			<Separator Classes="row-hairline" IsVisible="{Binding MenuSoundsAvailable}" />
			<Grid Classes="setting-row" ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" IsVisible="{Binding MenuSoundsAvailable}">
				<TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Classes="callout" Text="{l:Translate lblAudioMenuSounds}" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
				<ToggleSwitch Grid.Column="1" Name="chkAudioMenuSounds" IsChecked="{Binding Config.MenuSounds}" HorizontalAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
			</Grid>
		</StackPanel>
	</Border>
</UserControl>
